## Notebook/team workflow

Team environment is standardized around Conda environment `geocebada`, Python 3.11 and Jupyter kernel `Python (GeoCebada)`. See `docs/GETTING_STARTED.md`.

Local Conda file:

```text
environment.dev.yml
```

Standard install:

```bash
pip install -e ".[dev,geo]"
```

`environment.dev.yml` also installs GDAL and its NetCDF driver from conda-forge.
They are required before installing the optional `external` extra on Windows:
WaPOR otherwise falls back to an unsupported local C++ GDAL build and cannot
write its NetCDF products.

External raw-data contract: all contents below `data/raw/`, `data/interim/` and
`data/processed/` are ignored. Regenerate the versioned external-data inventory
with `python tools/build_external_data_manifest.py`; never commit raw rasters,
NetCDF files or manual-download CSVs.

Optional NVIDIA/CUDA 12 install:

```bash
pip install -e ".[dev,geo,gpu]"
```

The `gpu` extra installs `cupy-cuda12x`. GPU support is optional; code must retain a CPU path and must not require CUDA for CI or ordinary team use.

Do not require `sys.path` hacks, copied helpers or execution of another notebook first.

---

## Notebook status

`notebooks/01_visualizacion_datos.ipynb` is the lightweight first-look notebook: loaders, basic summaries, lightweight/rasterized pairplot, parcel-level descriptive view and `docs/VARIABLES.md` rendering.

`notebooks/02_cobertura_alineacion_temporal.ipynb` is the temporal workflow: train-vs-prediction coverage audit, weekly availability heatmap, configurable temporal grid, k-nearest-date alignment, gap/missingness diagnostics, aligned curves, one-row-per-parcel wide table and optional export to `data/interim/`.

The second notebook defaults to `*_promedio` variables and a 14-day grid to stay manageable, but can align all index statistics. It supports `BACKEND="auto"`, `cpu` or `gpu`.

